WEBVTT

00:00:15.907 --> 00:00:17.241
(ROARING)

00:00:33.925 --> 00:00:35.509
(CREDENCE YELLING)

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:09.251
(GASPS)

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.182
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.445
She's dead.

00:01:39.074 --> 00:01:41.075
How did the boy take it?

00:01:42.619 --> 00:01:44.036
He's sensitive.

00:01:45.997 --> 00:01:48.749
The Ministry won't be happy
when I tell them I missed.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.711
I know my reputation.

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:55.715
Listen to me. The disapproval of cowards
is praise to the brave.

00:01:56.842 --> 00:02:01.971
Your name will be written in glory
when wizards rule the world.

00:02:02.973 --> 00:02:05.307
And the clock is ticking faster.

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:09.729
You watch over Credence. Keep him safe.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:12.565
For the greater good.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.735
For the greater good.

00:02:16.319 --> 00:02:17.653
(COUPLE SPEAKING FRENCH)

00:02:18.822 --> 00:02:20.489
JACOB: You know what
I miss about Queenie?

00:02:23.118 --> 00:02:24.452
Everything.

00:02:26.955 --> 00:02:29.123
I even miss the stuff
that drove me nuts.

00:02:29.624 --> 00:02:31.125
Like the mind reading.

00:02:31.877 --> 00:02:33.294
(JACOB CHUCKLING)

00:02:36.339 --> 00:02:37.590
(JACOB SIGHS)

00:02:37.674 --> 00:02:42.219
I was lucky to have someone like her
even interested in anything I thought.

00:02:44.473 --> 00:02:46.056
You know what I mean?

00:02:47.142 --> 00:02:48.142
Sorry?

00:02:53.356 --> 00:02:56.650
I was saying, you're sure
the guy is here that we're looking for?

00:02:56.818 --> 00:02:59.320
Yeah, definitely. The feather says so.

00:02:59.404 --> 00:03:01.030
(FEATHER TAPPING GLASS)

00:03:14.044 --> 00:03:15.461
(EXHALES)

00:03:20.884 --> 00:03:22.718
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:03:25.388 --> 00:03:26.806
(TAPPING GLASS)

00:03:29.726 --> 00:03:30.976
JACOB: Is that the guy
we're looking for?

00:03:31.061 --> 00:03:32.061
NEWT: Yes.

00:03:34.481 --> 00:03:35.481
Ooh...

00:03:37.651 --> 00:03:38.651
Sorry.

00:03:39.486 --> 00:03:41.445
<i>Bonjour. Bonjour, monsieur.</i>

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:44.907
(IN ENGLISH) Oh, wait, no.
Sorry. So we actually...

00:03:45.075 --> 00:03:47.952
We were just wondering
if you'd come across a friend of ours.

00:03:48.703 --> 00:03:49.829
JACOB: Tina Goldstein.

00:03:50.288 --> 00:03:52.373
Monsieur, Paris is a large city.

00:03:52.457 --> 00:03:53.499
NEWT: She's an Auror.

00:03:54.751 --> 00:03:58.963
And when Aurors go missing,
the Ministry tend to come looking, so...

00:04:00.674 --> 00:04:03.634
No, I suppose it would probably
be better if we just report her absence.

00:04:04.135 --> 00:04:05.511
Is she tall?

00:04:07.138 --> 00:04:08.389
Dark? Rather...

00:04:08.557 --> 00:04:09.723
- Intense.
- Beautiful. She's...

00:04:10.642 --> 00:04:12.309
JACOB: Yeah, what I meant to say was...

00:04:12.477 --> 00:04:14.937
- No, she's very pretty.
- She's intense too.

00:04:15.689 --> 00:04:18.983
I think I saw
someone like this last night.

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:22.987
Perhaps if I showed you where...

00:04:23.154 --> 00:04:24.238
If you wouldn't mind. That would be...

00:04:25.574 --> 00:04:27.199
- That would be lovely.
- Sure.

00:04:59.274 --> 00:05:00.274
(JACOB CLEARING THROAT)

00:05:02.527 --> 00:05:03.861
(GASPS)

00:05:05.739 --> 00:05:06.864
Tina.

00:05:08.366 --> 00:05:09.491
Newt.

00:05:09.576 --> 00:05:10.743
<i>- YUSUF: Expelliarmus.</i>
- Oh!

00:05:12.037 --> 00:05:13.078
(ALL YELPING)

00:05:13.163 --> 00:05:16.123
My apologies, Mr. Scamander.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:20.169
I shall return and release you
once Credence is dead.

00:05:20.337 --> 00:05:21.337
Kama, wait.

00:05:21.504 --> 00:05:25.215
You see, either he dies or I do.

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:27.676
No, no, no.

00:05:27.844 --> 00:05:30.220
Oh, no. No, no, no.

00:05:30.305 --> 00:05:31.513
(GROANING)

00:05:32.557 --> 00:05:33.599
(THUDS)

00:05:40.565 --> 00:05:42.942
Well, that's not the best start
to a rescue attempt.

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:44.735
Oh, this was a rescue attempt?

00:05:44.903 --> 00:05:47.196
You just lost me my only lead.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:50.449
Well, how was the interrogation going
before we turned up?

00:05:51.034 --> 00:05:52.117
(PICKETT SQUEAKS)

00:05:52.202 --> 00:05:53.327
(JACOB LAUGHS)

00:05:53.787 --> 00:05:54.787
JACOB: Newt!

00:05:59.584 --> 00:06:00.709
Well done, Pick.

00:06:03.171 --> 00:06:04.922
So you need this man, you said?

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:06.799
Yeah.

00:06:06.967 --> 00:06:09.551
I think he knows
where Credence is, Mr. Scamander.

00:06:11.554 --> 00:06:13.389
(ZOUWU ROARING)

00:06:14.557 --> 00:06:16.100
Well, that'll be that Zouwu.

00:06:17.769 --> 00:06:19.853
- (ROARING)
- (PEOPLE SCREAMING)

